This project uses the @omni-design/components design system.

Read node_modules/@omni-design/components/CLAUDE.md before writing any UI.
It is the full contract; the rules below are the ones most often broken.
Also: docs/getting-started.md, docs/token-system.md, docs/components.md.

SETUP
- Import the CSS at the top of App.js:
    import '@omni-design/components/public/styles/foundation.css'
    import '@omni-design/components/public/styles/core.css'
    import '@omni-design/components/public/styles/Light-Mode.css'
    import '@omni-design/components/public/styles/base.css'
- Wrap content in an element with data-theme, data-surface and data-style.

COMPONENTS
- Import every UI element from '@omni-design/components'. No raw <button>,
  <input>, <select>, <input type="range">, <h1>-<h6>, <p>, or <a href>, and
  no '@mui/material' imports (MUI icons are fine).
- Missing component? Tag it — // MISSING-LIB-COMPONENT: <Name> — never fake
  one with a styled <div>.
- Anything that floats (menus, account panels, hover cards) is <Popover>.

COLOR AND SURFACES
- Never write hex colors or hard-coded radii. Use tokens.
- To paint a region, set data-theme + data-surface (or use <Section>);
  never background: var(--Surface) / var(--Container).
- Themes: Default, Primary, Secondary, Tertiary, Neutral, Info, Success,
  Warning, Error, App-Bar, Nav-Bar, Status. There are NO -Light / -Dark
  themes or button variants — lighter/darker is a surface level
  (Surface-Brightest / Surface-Dimmest).
- Surfaces: Surface-Dimmest, Surface-Dim, Surface, Surface-Bright,
  Surface-Brightest, and the Container levels.
- Styles: Professional, Modern, Bold, Playful.
- Navigation bars and rails use data-theme="App-Bar"; a phone bottom bar
  uses "Nav-Bar". Never pick a palette for navigation.
- Never pass style={{ color, background }} to a library component; use its
  variant or color prop.

DEVICES
- Set data-device on the root: IOS-Mobile, IOS-Tablet, Android-Mobile or
  Android-Tablet (Desktop is the default — set nothing). Type sizes switch on
  it, not on width.
- For responsive navigation use the Adaptive Nav add-on's exported file
  rather than assembling AppBar + Rail + BottomNavigation by hand.

LAYOUT
- Never center a container's text to center components inside it —
  text-align is inherited and centers their text too. Center the box.
